+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Order records are currently coupled to the lifecycle of their customer account, so deleting an account makes historical orders inaccessible to support staff. The admin order list also loses its pagination state after the first page, preventing reliable access to older orders.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Preserve the customer id, placed-with email, billing and delivery data, order status, history, and payment transactions needed to read and manage an order after its customer is deleted.
+- Allow the order detail endpoint and customer-order endpoint to serve historical orders without requiring a live customer row; returned orders have no customer object when the account no longer exists.
+- Make customer-order lookup filter directly by the recorded customer id, newest first, and return an empty list with `recordsTotal: 0` when there are no matches.
+- Correct admin order pagination so `page` is zero-based, filters are applied consistently, results are newest first, totals describe the filtered set, and out-of-range pages retain those totals.
+- Keep re-registration with a deleted email as a distinct account with no access to the deleted account's historical orders.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `historical-order-access`: Support durable retrieval and administration of orders independently of the current customer account.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+- None.
+
+## Impact
+
+The order API, order facade, order repository/service query and mapping layers, customer deletion/registration behavior, and automated tests covering order persistence and admin pagination are affected. No API route is removed; existing live-customer order responses should remain compatible.
